// @test: string reference-count registry exhaustion fails deterministically (#162)
// @env: VYB_STR_REG_CAP=16
// @expect: fail
// @expect-error: string reference-count registry exhausted
// @execute-jit: true
// @description: With the registry capacity forced low (16 slots) as a hard
//   ceiling, holding MORE strings LIVE than the table has slots (pushing each
//   fresh buffer into a Vec so none is freed) must exhaust the table. It must
//   fail loudly and deterministically instead of silently leaving an allocation
//   untracked (which would leak / corrupt reference counts).
//
//   NOTE: this holds the strings alive in a Vec. A pure reassignment-churn
//   loop (`s = s.concat(...)`) no longer exhausts a tiny table, because owned
//   temporary String arguments are now correctly released after the call
//   (#190/#191) -- churn reuses freed slots instead of filling the table.
main()<Int> -> {
    v<Vec<String>> = Vec<String>()
    i<Int> = 0
    while (i < 1000) {
        v.push(String::from_byte(i % 256))
        i += 1
    }
    return 0
}